1)	Removed routine 'go' and break_id_node, since they didn't work
	on the left side of assignments and they were a big hack anyway.
1.a)	Removed id_changed hack from toplev.c
1.b)	Removed 'break_id_node' from int.c
1.c)	Changed comment in intaux.c that refered to 'user' to 'usr'

2)	Changed the name of the directory the 'usr' package is stored into
	to be called 'usr', thus, hopefully in the long run, causing less
	confusion and allowing us to extend this to all the packages in
	the system.  [dump.c]

3)	Added a subroutine that can be called explicitly to dump the current
	environment as a text file.  First step at making export laundry.
	Don't use it yet. (You can't anyway, it's not implemented.)
	It will just bitch and complain if you do try it.
	[dump.c]

4)	Added additional comments to dump.c

5)	Removed ADA-to-C translator.  Didn't work and confused people.
	[cpp.c]

6)	Removed files, cpp.c and office.c, which were worthless and out-
	of-date.  [Makefile].

7)	Changed the name of the package uci_ada_functions to be uci.
	Too hard to type the old name.  The file name is still the same.
	[uci_ada_fns, user_package].

8)	Added
	  procedure die;	leaves the system without saving anything
				if croak_ok is true.
	  procedure export;	calls export laundry
	  procedure history(filename : string := "/dev/tty");
				writes a copy of every nodep that made it
				past the interpreter to the named file.
				This list grows without limit.  (It does
				anyway in the current system, since we
				never free internal form trees.)

	to package uci.

9)	Made the system always print memory statistics when it exits,
	since I think people should be aware of this for a while, at least.
9 1/2)	Made a new routine, quick_memreport, that only prints the total
	usage, since memreport talks too much.  [misc.c, init.c]

10)	Moved maptab from dump.c to misc.c.

11)	misc.c got screwed up somehow.  The version numbers went 

	most recent: 1.3 (same 1.2.4.1) 
	next most recent 1.3.4.1.  

	Presumably at some point someone took out the stuff they had
	put in for constrp's, since there is no such thing in the
	current system.  But misc.c didn't know that and still had code
	in it that referenced constrp's.  How this happened I don't
	know.  Probably no one noticed because misc.c is recompiled
	rather infrequently.  I took all that out and also deleted the
	log entry that said it was ever put in. [misc.c]

12)	Changed the indentation of the uses list in the 'dir' command
	to match the rest of the listing.  [dir.c].

13)	Taught procedure dir to print the contents of functions and
	procedures as well as packages.  Also changed the headers it
	printed for the body and visible part to be more descriptive.
	(visible: -> package specification:, body: -> package
	implementation:, and added subprogram:.) [dir.c].

14)	Changed the formatting of the dir procedure to print
	fewer newlines, since more will fit on a screen that way.  I
	changed the routine dirsym to not print newlines at the end of
	each symbol.  I changed the dir routine to print three on a
	line, but the formatting isn't perfect, since I can't get
	the length of each thing that dirsym prints very easily.  I
	dunno, I might change this back.  I had to also change ppcref.c
	since it called fdirsym which called dirsym which it assumed
	would print a newline. [dir.c, ppcref.c].

15)	Put back in del procedure.  The cheap way it works for now is
	to merely set the class of the fixform to be undef_id.  The
	symbol isn't actually deleted.  Made dir procedure print them as
	<deleted>.  This should be changed to actually delete the
	symbol.  Also, modified del routine to only work from toplevel,
	otherwise havoc could result, because the fixp bindings are
	only updated every time we hit the top level.

16)	New flag "write_core_file", which is the new default argument
	to "quit."  If true, then a "save" will be done whenever quit
	is invoked.  The idea is to keep ADA.SAVE and ada.core in sync.
	If you call quit with this argument true, then quit must be
	called from the toplevel (since the same is true of "save"); an
	error will be reported if this isn't the case.

17)	xxdebugflag in int.h should be removed before the next system
	build.  I left it in because I didn't want to check out int.h.
	It isn't referenced anywhere anymore.

18)	The bug with creating the 'usr' directory seems to have gone away.

19)	I made redefining identifiers in 'usr' a lot more reliable,
	though it still isn't perfect.  I put in some

		f->fxf.class = class;

	statements.  Before, if you did something like type in a
	procedure, called 'p', and then redefined 'p' to be a type
	definition, everything got royally screwed up.  Now that
	happens less often.

20)	Added subroutine 'touch' which, when given a symbol, makes sure that
	it has been swapped into the system.  Changed do_ident to call this,
	and also made it available via an Ada procedure.
	[uci_ada_fns, init.c, symtab.c, intaux.c].

21)	Moved and renamed subroutine top_level_error to check_top_level and
	put it in misc.c.  [init.c, misc.c]

22)	Renamed procedure psyms to be printall, since that is the internal
	name.  I think maybe it should go away altogether, since we have
	better printing tools.

23)	Changed the name of dir to ls and del to rm.  More Unix-like.
	Why should be emulate a dinosaur like tops-20?

24)	There was an error in the old dir (now ls) specification, in that
	it never referenced ls_color, instead assuming no_color.

25)	Undid change # 14:  everything prints in single columns again.
	Note the following definition of dir that you can use if you want:
	  procedure dir(s : symbol := usr'sym) is begin
	     dir(s, filename => ",dirfile");
	     csh("more ,dirfile");
	  end;

26)	Undid 1/2 of change # 23: dir is still dir, but del is rm.
